{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_04-a2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_04-a2", "base_text": "Small animals like birds, squirrels, mice and insects are a common sight in many cities and towns. But in recent years, the world's press has been full of reports of wild animals coming into cities in bigger and bigger numbers. There have been bears in Vancouver parks, leopards on the streets of Mumbai and wild pigs in gardens in Berlin. What happens when bigger animals come into our cities? Are they welcome or are they considered a danger or a pest?", "probe_text": "Little animals like birds, squirrels, mice and insects are a frequent sight in many cities and towns. But in recent years, the world's press has been full of reports of wild animals coming into cities in bigger and bigger numbers. There have been bears in Vancouver parks, leopards on the streets of Mumbai and wild pigs in gardens in Berlin. What happens when bigger animals come into our cities? Are they welcome or are they considered a danger or a pest?", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "Small→Little;common→frequent", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.96,ratio=1.00"}
