{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_11-a2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_11-a2", "base_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a common language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can result in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could help stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "probe_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a common language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can consequence in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could aid stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "help→aid;result→consequence", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.97,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_11-b1", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_11-b1", "base_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a common language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can result in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could help stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "probe_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a widespread language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can consequence in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could help stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "target_level": "b1", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "common→widespread;result→consequence", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.97,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_12-a2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_12-a2", "base_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language?", "probe_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we launch to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains launch producing language?", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "start→launch;start→launch", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.98,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_12-b1", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_12-b1", "base_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language?", "probe_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we commence to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains commence producing language?", "target_level": "b1", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "start→commence;start→commence", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.98,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_14-a2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_14-a2", "base_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few people in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "probe_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few citizens in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "people→citizens", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.99,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_14-b1", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_14-b1", "base_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few people in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "probe_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few individuals in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "target_level": "b1", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "people→individuals", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.99,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_LEX_TSAR_15-a2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "lexical", "base_item_id": "TSAR_15-a2", "base_text": "On the basis of these findings, we recommend that Girox Foods adopt a more people-oriented management style. As part of this, we should explore ways of offering more flexible working hours to our employees and consider how we can enable employees to work from their chosen locations. Managers need to consider a variety of ways to challenge our staff and provide more positive reinforcement and recognition of the work they do. Increased investment in professional development, especially in the area of social and intercultural communication, could also contribute to creating a positive environment for employees to produce their best work.", "probe_text": "On the basis of these findings, we recommend that Girox Foods adopt a more people-oriented management style. As part of this, we should explore ways of offering more flexible working hours to our employees and consider how we can enable employees to work from their chosen locations. Managers need to consider a variety of ways to challenge our staff and supply more positive reinforcement and recognition of the work they do. Increased investment in professional development, especially in the region of social and intercultural communication, could also contribute to creating a positive environment for employees to produce their best work.", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "area→region;provide→supply", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "rule_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.97,ratio=1.00"}
