{"probe_id": "SC_TSAR_06-a2", "probe_family": "shortcut", "probe_subtype": "detail_generic_qualifying", "base_item_id": "TSAR_06-a2", "base_text": "One night in 2003, Suzanne Collins was flipping between channels on TV. It was at the time of the US invasion of Iraq. The only programmes she could find on TV were 'reality' programmes of young people competing to win a million dollars and news programmes about the war. Suzanne says that the two things start to merge together in a disturbing way and the idea for The Hunger Games came to her.", "probe_text": "One night in 2003, Suzanne Collins was flipping between channels on TV. It was at the time of the US invasion of Iraq. The only programmes she could find on TV were 'reality' programmes of young people competing to win a million dollars and news programmes about the war. Suzanne says that the two things start to merge together in a disturbing way and the idea for The Hunger Games came to her, which experts say could worsen without intervention.", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "no_shortcut", "critical_detail": "which experts say could worsen without intervention", "operation": "generic_qualifying: \"which experts say could worsen without intervention\"", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "template_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "template"}
