{"probe_id": "SC_TSAR_12-a2", "probe_family": "shortcut", "probe_subtype": "detail_generic_qualifying", "base_item_id": "TSAR_12-a2", "base_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language?", "probe_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language, particularly during extreme weather events.", "target_level": "a2", "expected_relation": "no_shortcut", "critical_detail": "particularly during extreme weather events", "operation": "generic_qualifying: \"particularly during extreme weather events\"", "tier": 1, "dataset": "TSAR2025", "generator_model": "template_based", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "template"}
