{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0316", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0316", "base_text": "The West Coast blues is a type of blues music characterized by jazz and jump blues influences, strong piano-dominated sounds and jazzy guitar solos, which originated from Texas blues players relocated to California in the 1940s.", "probe_text": "The West Coast blues style draws heavily on jazz and jump blues traditions, marked by a distinctive blend of powerful piano-driven melodies and improvisational guitar solos with a distinctly jazzy flair. Its roots can be traced back to Texas musicians who migrated to California in the 1940s, bringing their unique musical influences with them.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.62,ratio=1.50"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0321", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0321", "base_text": "The British Rail Class 91 is a class of 140 mph (225 km / h), 4.54MW / 6,300 hp electric locomotives ordered as a component of the East Coast Main Line modernisation and electrification programme of the late 1980s.", "probe_text": "As part of the East Coast Main Line's renovation and electrical upgrade scheme in the late 1980s, the British Rail Class 91 locomotives were commissioned - a class of high-speed electric engines capable of reaching speeds of up to 225 km/h or 140 mph, producing 4.54MW of power equivalent to approximately 6,300 horsepower.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.74,ratio=1.36"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0329", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0329", "base_text": "Adrastea was discovered by David C. Jewitt and G. Edward Danielson in Voyager 2 probe photographs taken on July 8, 1979, and received the designation.", "probe_text": "Photographs from Voyager 2 probe were examined by astronomers David C. Jewitt and G. Edward Danielson, revealing Adrastea's presence for the first time in images captured on July 8, 1979, earning it its official classification.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.76,ratio=1.40"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0337", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0337", "base_text": "He was holidaying in Germany the following summer when World War I broke out.", "probe_text": "The following summer, he had traveled to Germany for a vacation when hostilities erupted as World War I began.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 2, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.64,ratio=1.36"}
