{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0460", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0460", "base_text": "In addition to the town Gouda in the Netherlands, Gouda can refer to: Gouda (cheese) Gouda (pottery) Gouda (slang) Gouda, South Africa, a town in the Western Cape Province of South Africa.", "probe_text": "Beyond Gouda in the Netherlands, the term 'Gouda' also encompasses: The cheese originating from this Dutch town. A type of pottery made or sold there. Slang used to describe something excellent or impressive. Alternatively, a small town located within South Africa's Western Cape Province.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 2, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.84,ratio=1.38"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0461", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0461", "base_text": "TPL then sold a conservation easement over the entire property to the state of Florida, while Polk County purchased the gardens portion of the property, less the development rights conveyed in the state easement.", "probe_text": "The Trust for Public Land (TPL) subsequently transferred its interest in a conservation easement covering the entire estate to the State of Florida. At the same time, Polk County acquired ownership of the gardens portion of the property, excluding those development rights previously surrendered as part of the state-held easement.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.72,ratio=1.47"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0462", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0462", "base_text": "In common with The Beatles, they came from Liverpool and were managed by Brian Epstein.", "probe_text": "Like The Beatles, they hailed from Liverpool, with their career being overseen by Brian Epstein.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.60,ratio=1.00"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0476", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0476", "base_text": "By 2003, the Wi-Fi Alliance announced that WEP had been superseded by Wi-Fi Protected Access (WPA), which was a subset of then upcoming 802.11i amendment.", "probe_text": "By 2003, the Wi-Fi Alliance declared that WEP was rendered obsolete in favor of Wi-Fi Protected Access (WPA), a component of the forthcoming 802.11i standard revision.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.61,ratio=1.04"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0482", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0482", "base_text": "As well as current kit sponsors for Bayern Munich, Ferencvárosi TC, and West Bromwich Albion, T-Mobile were co-sponsors of Everton with the One2One brand and they also sponsored the 2002 FA Youth Cup Final.", "probe_text": "In addition to their partnerships with current kit suppliers for Bayern Munich, Ferencvárosi TC, and West Bromwich Albion, T-Mobile was a co-backer of Everton under the One2One brand, and they also supported the 2002 FA Youth Cup Final.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.84,ratio=1.12"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0483", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0483", "base_text": "The bridge now traverses the Tarn valley above its lowest point, linking two limestone plateaux, the Causse du Larzac and the Causse Rouge, and is inside the perimeter of the Grands Causses regional natural park.", "probe_text": "Sitting atop its deepest low-lying point, the bridge now spans the Tarn valley, bridging the Causse Rouge and the Causse du Larzac, two adjacent limestone plateaux, while lying within the boundaries of the Grands Causses regional natural park.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.75,ratio=1.09"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0486", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0486", "base_text": "It comprises the eastern half of the island of Timor, the nearby islands of Atauro and Jaco, and Oecussi-Ambeno, an exclave on the northwestern side of the island, within Indonesian West Timor.", "probe_text": "The area encompasses the eastern segment of Timor Island, along with the adjacent islets of Atauro and Jaco. It also includes Oecussi-Ambeno, a distinct territorial entity situated on the northwestern coast, geographically isolated within West Timor in Indonesia.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 2, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.65,ratio=1.19"}
