{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-8b_ASSET_val_0811", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0811", "base_text": "After the mutiny Following the Indian Mutiny of 1857 - 58 and the consequent abolition of the East India Company, its European regiments were amalgamated in 1860 with the British Army, but its ‘ Native ’ regiments were not.", "probe_text": "In the aftermath of the 1857-58 Indian Rebellion, when the British East India Company was dissolved and its remnants dismantled, the European components of its military forces were merged into the regular British Army in 1860. However, its indigenous units, commonly referred to as 'Native' regiments, continued to exist independently at that time.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-8b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.62,ratio=1.36"}
