{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_gemma-3-27b_ASSET_val_0434", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0434", "base_text": "In biology and demography, fecundity is the potential reproductive capacity of an organism or population, measured by the number of gametes (eggs), seed set or asexual propagules.", "probe_text": "Reproductive capacity, referred to as fecundity in biological and population studies, is determined by quantifying the number of gametes produced—such as eggs—or the quantity of seeds or asexual offspring.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by gemma-3-27b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.62,ratio=1.07"}
