{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_gemma-3-27b_ASSET_val_0985", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0985", "base_text": "Retrieved 2008 - 12 - 25 Album information The title of the album, \"A Little Bit Longer\", comes from their song of the same name, which Nick Jonas wrote about his dealings with having type 1 diabetes.", "probe_text": "Information regarding the album was accessed on December 25, 2008. The album's name, “A Little Bit Longer,” is derived from a song sharing that title, penned by Nick Jonas reflecting on his experiences living with type 1 diabetes.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by gemma-3-27b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.63,ratio=1.03"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_gemma-3-27b_ASSET_val_0991", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0991", "base_text": "Individual songs from some of the operettas have become standards, notably \"Vilja\" from The Merry Widow and \"You Are My Heart's Delight\" (\"Dein ist mein ganzes Herz\") from The Land of Smiles.", "probe_text": "Certain operetta pieces have achieved lasting popularity as well-known songs, including “Vilja” from The Merry Widow and “You Are My Heart’s Delight” (“Dein ist mein ganzes Herz”) originating from The Land of Smiles.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by gemma-3-27b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.79,ratio=1.03"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_gemma-3-27b_ASSET_val_0992", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0992", "base_text": "The fourth and fifth digits designate the number of the urban area (in a district-free city) or the district (in a city with districts).", "probe_text": "The digits in the fourth and fifth positions indicate whether the location is a city without districts, specifying the urban area number, or a city divided into districts, identifying the district number.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by gemma-3-27b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.78,ratio=1.33"}
