{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_gemma-3-27b_ASSET_val_1511", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1511", "base_text": "The habitable zone (HZ) in astronomy is a region of space where stellar conditions are favorable for life as it is found on Earth.", "probe_text": "In astronomy, the region known as the habitable zone—or HZ—is the area around a star where conditions could allow for the existence of life forms similar to those on Earth.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by gemma-3-27b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.74,ratio=1.25"}
{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_gemma-3-27b_ASSET_val_1514", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1514", "base_text": "Suggested etiologies of the name \"Kavirondo\" include From local young warriors, armed with spears, bows, arrows, & clubs, who were observed to sit on their heels, which in Kiswahili is kaa virondo.", "probe_text": "Possible origins of the name \"Kavirondo\" propose it derives from observations of local, youthful fighters—equipped with spears, bows, arrows, and clubs—who habitually knelt on their heels, a posture described as *kaa virondo* in the Kiswahili language.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by gemma-3-27b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.61,ratio=1.12"}
