{"probe_id": "INV_SEM_llama-3.1-70b_ASSET_val_0779", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_0779", "base_text": "The first minaret was constructed in 665 in Basra during the reign of the Umayyad caliph Muawiyah I. Muawiyah encouraged the construction of minarets, as they were supposed to bring mosques on par with Christian churches with their bell towers.", "probe_text": "The construction of the initial minaret took place in 665, within the city of Basra, under the rule of Umayyad caliph Muawiyah I. By promoting the building of minarets, Muawiyah aimed to elevate mosques to a similar stature as Christian churches, which were distinguished by their bell towers.", "target_level": "simpler", "expected_relation": "stable", "operation": "paraphrase by llama-3.1-70b", "tier": 1, "dataset": "ASSET", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "rule_pass": true, "rule_detail": "recall=0.62,ratio=1.20"}
