{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_TSAR_09-a2_a02290b7", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_09-a2", "base_text": "Some bridge collapses are mysteries, and engineers only realise why after they conduct a complete investigation. In some cases, this could happen because inferior-quality material was used in the construction, or because of a defect in a key piece of the bridge. In other cases, the bridge was designed only to support a certain amount of weight and no more.", "probe_text": "Certain bridge collapses remain enigmas until engineers undertake an exhaustive inquiry to uncover the cause. The root of the problem may lie in the use of substandard materials during construction or a flaw in a critical component of the bridge's structure. Alternatively, the bridge's design may have been intended to bear only a specific load capacity, beyond which it is unable to withstand additional weight.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
