{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1551_aabb29bd", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1551", "base_text": "Pethidine is also relatively contraindicated for use when a patient is suffering from liver, or kidney disease, has a history of seizures or epilepsy, has an enlarged prostate or urinary retention problems, or suffers from hypothyroidism, asthma, or Addison's disease.", "probe_text": "Pethidine should generally be avoided in patients who have liver or kidney disorders, a past history of seizures or epilepsy, an enlarged prostate or issues with urinary retention, or who are affected by hypothyroidism, asthma, or Addison's disease.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1552_da0701ef", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1552", "base_text": "When wells are lost to pollution, there is no town water which can be brought in because the town government has no wells of its own.", "probe_text": "If wells become contaminated, there is no municipal water available, since the local government does not possess any wells itself.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1548_65c075d2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1548", "base_text": "Werner Heisenberg (5 December 1901 – 1 February 1976) was a German theoretical physicist who made foundational contributions to quantum mechanics and is best known for asserting the uncertainty principle of quantum theory.", "probe_text": "Werner Heisenberg (December 5, 1901 – February 1, 1976) was a German theoretical physicist recognized for his fundamental work in quantum mechanics and is most famous for formulating the uncertainty principle in quantum theory.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1553_15579e7e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1553", "base_text": "Cherryade was first produced in the 19th century, along with other beverages such as limeade and ginger beer, which had come about due to the popularity of lemonade.", "probe_text": "Cherryade originated in the 19th century, alongside drinks like limeade and ginger beer, which emerged because lemonade had become popular.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1563_bfcff55f", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1563", "base_text": "Trohman was a poor fit for the band in terms of familiarity with the music and in terms of stage presence.", "probe_text": "Trohman did not suit the band well, both because he was unfamiliar with the music and lacked stage presence.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1564_2f750a1e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1564", "base_text": "Koop was a somewhat eccentric and flamboyant figure, well-known for his mustache-less beard and colorful bow ties.", "probe_text": "Koop was known for being a rather unconventional and striking personality, famous for his beard without a mustache and his vibrant bow ties.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_01-b1_686f2ef8", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_01-b1", "base_text": "Now NASA is working towards logging some of the smaller asteroids, those measuring 140 metres wide or more. Of the 25,000 estimated asteroids of this size, so far about 8,000 have been logged, leaving 17,000 unaccounted for. Considering that a 19-metre asteroid that exploded above the city of Chelyabinsk in Russia in 2013 injured 1,200 people, these middle-sized asteroids would be a serious danger if they enter Earth's orbit.", "probe_text": "Currently, NASA is focused on cataloging smaller asteroids with diameters exceeding 140 meters. Out of approximately 25,000 estimated asteroids of this size, roughly 8,000 have been documented so far, leaving around 17,000 unidentified. Given that a 19-meter asteroid's explosion over Chelyabinsk in Russia in 2013 caused injuries to over 1,200 people, mid-sized asteroids entering Earth's orbit pose a significant threat.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_01-a2_8987bb82", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_01-a2", "base_text": "Now NASA is working towards logging some of the smaller asteroids, those measuring 140 metres wide or more. Of the 25,000 estimated asteroids of this size, so far about 8,000 have been logged, leaving 17,000 unaccounted for. Considering that a 19-metre asteroid that exploded above the city of Chelyabinsk in Russia in 2013 injured 1,200 people, these middle-sized asteroids would be a serious danger if they enter Earth's orbit.", "probe_text": "NASA is currently focusing on cataloging smaller asteroids with diameters of at least 140 meters. Out of an estimated 25,000 such objects, roughly 8,000 have been documented so far, leaving around 17,000 unidentified. Given that a relatively small asteroid measuring just 19 meters in diameter caused significant damage and injury when it detonated above Chelyabinsk, Russia in 2013, the threat posed by these mid-sized asteroids is substantial should they enter Earth's orbit.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_04-a2_150c2482", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_04-a2", "base_text": "Small animals like birds, squirrels, mice and insects are a common sight in many cities and towns. But in recent years, the world's press has been full of reports of wild animals coming into cities in bigger and bigger numbers. There have been bears in Vancouver parks, leopards on the streets of Mumbai and wild pigs in gardens in Berlin. What happens when bigger animals come into our cities? Are they welcome or are they considered a danger or a pest?", "probe_text": "In urban areas such as cities and towns, it's not unusual to spot small creatures like birds, squirrels, mice, and insects going about their daily business. However, over the past few years, news outlets worldwide have been filled with stories of wild animals venturing into metropolitan areas in increasing numbers. From Vancouver's parks to Mumbai's streets and Berlin's gardens, sightings of bears, leopards, and wild boars have become more frequent. When larger wildlife enters our cities, do they receive a warm welcome or are they viewed as threats or nuisances?", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_03-b1_c7f8552b", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_03-b1", "base_text": "The Hunger Games are an annual event, which the Capitol uses to remind the districts that they are being punished for rebelling. Every year one boy and one girl aged 12 to 18 are chosen from each district by lottery to compete in a battle in which only one person can survive. The chosen teenagers are called \"tributes\". The whole nation is forced to watch the event on television.", "probe_text": "Each year, the Capitol orchestrates a nationwide spectacle as a stern reminder of the districts' past defiance. This annual event selects two participants from each district through a random draw, aged 12 to 18, who are then compelled to participate in a brutal competition where only one can emerge victorious. The selected adolescents are designated as \"tributes\", while the entire nation is coerced into witnessing the ordeal on television broadcasts.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1565_34a4ceee", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1565", "base_text": "It is the third-largest subdivision of China spanning about 1,200,000 km ² (463,000 sq mi) or 12% of China's land area.", "probe_text": "Covering roughly 1,200,000 km² (463,000 sq mi) or 12% of China's total land area, it ranks as the country's third-largest subdivision.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_05-b1_05375a25", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_05-b1", "base_text": "Potentially Hazardous Asteroids' are rocks close enough to pass within 7.5 million kilometres of Earth's orbit. NASA has created a map of 1,400 PHAs, none of which are expected to be a threat in the next one hundred years. With technology already available, NASA can track these objects and make predictions about possible impact, at which point two defence solutions could be launched.", "probe_text": "Asteroids classified as potentially hazardous are situated within a 7.5 million kilometre radius of Earth's orbital path. A comprehensive map has been developed by NASA to identify approximately 1,400 such asteroids, none of which pose an imminent threat over the next century. Leveraging existing technology, NASA is capable of monitoring these objects and forecasting potential collision scenarios, thereby enabling the deployment of two defensive strategies in response.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_08-b1_cdf83bc8", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_08-b1", "base_text": "Dreams of a phone call from an old friend or the death of someone close, for example, are more likely to be the result of coincidence than prophecy. And, of course, we probably choose to forget all the times we dream about such events but they don't happen.", "probe_text": "Incidents like a long-lost friend's phone call or a loved one's passing, often feature in our dreams, yet it's more probable that these are mere coincidences rather than harbingers of future events. Moreover, we tend to overlook the numerous instances where such dream scenarios fail to materialize.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1568_3d7293a9", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1568", "base_text": "Current stations Most stations are named for the nearest major road crossed by the line in question.", "probe_text": "Present stations are typically named after the closest major road that the line intersects.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1562_447073d6", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1562", "base_text": "Despite their similarity to members of the genus Mus, scientists suspect that the African spiny mice may be more closely related to gerbils than to common mice.", "probe_text": "Although African spiny mice resemble species in the genus Mus, researchers believe they are more closely related to gerbils than to typical mice.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_06-b1_c5b0753b", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_06-b1", "base_text": "One night in 2003, Suzanne Collins was flipping between channels on TV. It was at the time of the US invasion of Iraq. The only programmes she could find on TV were 'reality' programmes of young people competing to win a million dollars and news programmes about the war. Suzanne says that the two things start to merge together in a disturbing way and the idea for The Hunger Games came to her.", "probe_text": "In 2003, Suzanne Collins was channel surfing on television one evening. This coincided with the US-led invasion of Iraq. As she flipped through channels, she found herself stuck between two types of programming - reality TV shows where contestants vied for a million-dollar prize and news broadcasts detailing the war's progress. According to Collins, these disparate elements began to blur together in an unsettling manner, ultimately inspiring the concept behind The Hunger Games.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_02-b1_b6c04242", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_02-b1", "base_text": "Earthquakes damage all structures, including bridges. Luckily, this kind of collapse is relatively infrequent, especially with modern bridges. Engineers have learned to design bridges in earthquake zones on areas that are much more resistant to movement.", "probe_text": "Bridges and other constructions suffer significant damage from earthquakes. Fortunately, such catastrophic failures are rare occurrences, particularly when it comes to contemporary bridge architecture. By studying seismic activity patterns, engineers have developed expertise in designing bridges in high-risk zones that can withstand intense ground movements.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1570_8352938a", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1570", "base_text": "Platform game, or platformer, is a video game genre characterized by jumping to and from suspended platforms or over obstacles.", "probe_text": "A platformer, also known as a platform game, is a type of video game defined by the player jumping between elevated platforms or across barriers.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1574_8a01af38", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1574", "base_text": "This was named by the English, but the megalithic mound significantly predates them.", "probe_text": "The English gave it this name, although the megalithic mound existed long before their time.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_06-a2_0e108a91", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_06-a2", "base_text": "One night in 2003, Suzanne Collins was flipping between channels on TV. It was at the time of the US invasion of Iraq. The only programmes she could find on TV were 'reality' programmes of young people competing to win a million dollars and news programmes about the war. Suzanne says that the two things start to merge together in a disturbing way and the idea for The Hunger Games came to her.", "probe_text": "In 2003, a pivotal moment struck Suzanne Collins as she channel-surfed through TV broadcasts. Coinciding with the US-led invasion of Iraq, Collins was bombarded by two distinct types of programming - reality shows where contestants vied for a million-dollar prize and news reports detailing the war's unfolding drama. As she flipped between these contrasting narratives, Collins reveals that they began to blur together in a disquieting manner, ultimately giving rise to the concept that would become The Hunger Games.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1575_33d7ca70", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1575", "base_text": "It had maximum sustained winds of, and a minimum pressure of 1002 mbar.", "probe_text": "Its peak sustained winds reached, with a lowest pressure recorded at 1002 mbar.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_03-a2_d0125248", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_03-a2", "base_text": "The Hunger Games are an annual event, which the Capitol uses to remind the districts that they are being punished for rebelling. Every year one boy and one girl aged 12 to 18 are chosen from each district by lottery to compete in a battle in which only one person can survive. The chosen teenagers are called \"tributes\". The whole nation is forced to watch the event on television.", "probe_text": "Every year, the Capitol orchestrates a high-stakes spectacle known as the Hunger Games, designed to serve as a stark reminder of the districts' rebellion and its consequences. As part of this ritual, 12-18 year olds from each district are randomly selected through a lottery system to participate in a brutal fight-to-the-death competition, where only one participant will emerge victorious. Those chosen for this perilous task are referred to as \"tributes\". The entire nation is coerced into witnessing the event on television, forced to bear witness to the gruesome spectacle.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1576_f04b4346", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1576", "base_text": "Ideas and works that are reproducible at zero cost, or almost zero cost.", "probe_text": "Concepts and creations that can be duplicated for free or for nearly no expense.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_07-a2_cbe8e2cc", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_07-a2", "base_text": "The Life of Pi tells the extraordinary story of Pi, a teenage boy from India, who is shipwrecked and finds himself trapped in a lifeboat in the Pacific Ocean with a ferocious tiger. It is the third book by the Canadian author Yann Martel, and was published in 2001. Since then, it has sold over seven million copies worldwide, won several prizes and been translated into 41 languages. Martel is the son of a diplomat and as a child lived in Costa Rica, Canada, France and Mexico.", "probe_text": "Yann Martel's novel, The Life of Pi, recounts an extraordinary tale about Pi, a young Indian boy who finds himself stranded on a lifeboat in the Pacific Ocean alongside a formidable tiger after being shipwrecked. This was Martel's third published book, released in 2001, and it has since become a global bestseller with over seven million copies sold worldwide, earning numerous awards and being translated into forty-one languages. Born to a diplomat father, Martel spent his childhood in various countries including Costa Rica, Canada, France, and Mexico.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1584_aa7a70ec", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1584", "base_text": "Location and habitat The area most populated by this fish is at the junction of the Amazon River and the Rio Negro, near Brazil's inland city of Manaus.", "probe_text": "Habitat and location This fish is most commonly found where the Amazon River meets the Rio Negro, close to the inland Brazilian city of Manaus.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_04-b1_63c2f125", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_04-b1", "base_text": "Small animals like birds, squirrels, mice and insects are a common sight in many cities and towns. But in recent years, the world's press has been full of reports of wild animals coming into cities in bigger and bigger numbers. There have been bears in Vancouver parks, leopards on the streets of Mumbai and wild pigs in gardens in Berlin. What happens when bigger animals come into our cities? Are they welcome or are they considered a danger or a pest?", "probe_text": "In urban areas such as cities and towns, it's not uncommon to spot small creatures like birds, squirrels, mice, and insects going about their daily business. However, in recent times, the media has been flooded with stories of wild animals venturing into metropolitan areas in increasing numbers. From bears roaming Vancouver parks to leopards prowling Mumbai streets and wild boars rooting around Berlin gardens, the trend is unmistakable. But what happens when larger wildlife enters our cities? Are these visitors viewed as welcome guests or are they seen as a threat or nuisance?", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1585_73f7c5f7", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1585", "base_text": "He has composed and arranged scores for more than 500 film and television productions.", "probe_text": "He has written and arranged music for over 500 movies and TV shows.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1581_4fd0709d", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1581", "base_text": "With 27.7% of the daily crude oil production halted due to the depression, oil prices rose further after days of increasing levels, and on September 20 reached a record rate of over $84 per barrel.", "probe_text": "As a result of the depression stopping 27.7% of daily crude oil output, oil prices continued to climb after several days of increases, hitting a new high of more than $84 per barrel on September 20.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_07-b1_bf9f667a", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_07-b1", "base_text": "The Life of Pi tells the extraordinary story of Pi, a teenage boy from India, who is shipwrecked and finds himself trapped in a lifeboat in the Pacific Ocean with a ferocious tiger. It is the third book by the Canadian author Yann Martel, and was published in 2001. Since then, it has sold over seven million copies worldwide, won several prizes and been translated into 41 languages. Martel is the son of a diplomat and as a child lived in Costa Rica, Canada, France and Mexico.", "probe_text": "In \"The Life of Pi\", Yann Martel masterfully recounts the incredible journey of Pi, a young Indian boy who finds himself stranded on a lifeboat in the vast Pacific Ocean alongside a formidable tiger. This captivating novel marks Canadian author Martel's third literary endeavour, first hitting bookshelves in 2001. The book has since achieved remarkable success, selling over seven million copies globally and earning numerous accolades, with translations into an impressive 41 languages. Born to a diplomat father, Martel spent his childhood navigating diverse cultures, having lived in Costa Rica, Canada, France, and Mexico.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_02-a2_fc76b7a7", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_02-a2", "base_text": "Earthquakes damage all structures, including bridges. Luckily, this kind of collapse is relatively infrequent, especially with modern bridges. Engineers have learned to design bridges in earthquake zones on areas that are much more resistant to movement.", "probe_text": "Bridges and other infrastructure suffer significant damage during earthquakes. Fortunately, such catastrophic failures are rare occurrences, particularly when it comes to contemporary bridge construction. By studying seismic activity, engineers can now build bridges in high-risk areas with enhanced stability against ground movements.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1591_9ed817ee", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1591", "base_text": "The forecasters then stated that Franklin could \"attain and maintain hurricane strength\" and make a close approach to Bermuda.", "probe_text": "The forecasters later mentioned that Franklin might \"reach and sustain hurricane intensity\" and come near Bermuda.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1592_e83a8898", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1592", "base_text": "In Shinto worship, the kami are invited to leave Takama-ga-hara and enter a shrine or some other purified place.", "probe_text": "During Shinto rituals, the kami are summoned from Takama-ga-hara to inhabit a shrine or another cleansed location.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_05-a2_a442bdc9", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_05-a2", "base_text": "Potentially Hazardous Asteroids' are rocks close enough to pass within 7.5 million kilometres of Earth's orbit. NASA has created a map of 1,400 PHAs, none of which are expected to be a threat in the next one hundred years. With technology already available, NASA can track these objects and make predictions about possible impact, at which point two defence solutions could be launched.", "probe_text": "Asteroids posing a potential hazard to Earth are situated within 7.5 million kilometres of our planet's orbital path. A comprehensive map has been compiled by NASA of approximately 1,400 such objects, none of which are forecasted to pose a threat in the immediate future, i.e., over the next century. Leveraging existing technological capabilities, NASA is able to monitor these asteroids and make informed predictions regarding potential collision courses, at which juncture two defensive strategies could be implemented.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_08-a2_bcb8f25e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_08-a2", "base_text": "Dreams of a phone call from an old friend or the death of someone close, for example, are more likely to be the result of coincidence than prophecy. And, of course, we probably choose to forget all the times we dream about such events but they don't happen.", "probe_text": "It's unlikely that dreams foretelling a phone call from an old acquaintance or the passing of someone dear are more than mere coincidences. Moreover, it's probable that we tend to overlook instances where we've dreamed about similar events only to find them never materializing.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1600_ad31214e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1600", "base_text": "It involved the WCW wrestlers \"invading\" WWF television in an attempt to \"take over\" the WWF.", "probe_text": "The storyline featured WCW wrestlers appearing on WWF television, trying to \"take control\" of the WWF.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_09-a2_4302322e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_09-a2", "base_text": "Some bridge collapses are mysteries, and engineers only realise why after they conduct a complete investigation. In some cases, this could happen because inferior-quality material was used in the construction, or because of a defect in a key piece of the bridge. In other cases, the bridge was designed only to support a certain amount of weight and no more.", "probe_text": "Engineers often uncover the reasons behind bridge collapses after conducting thorough investigations, which can reveal surprising causes. Sometimes, the collapse is attributed to subpar materials used in the construction process or a critical flaw in one of its components. In other instances, the bridge's design was inherently limited by its capacity to support only a specific weight load.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1601_18a36bc2", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1601", "base_text": "The riot continued into the early morning, until police used fire brigade water hoses to disperse the crowd.", "probe_text": "The unrest lasted into the early hours, ending only when police broke up the crowd with fire department water hoses.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_09-b1_32425aea", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_09-b1", "base_text": "Some bridge collapses are mysteries, and engineers only realise why after they conduct a complete investigation. In some cases, this could happen because inferior-quality material was used in the construction, or because of a defect in a key piece of the bridge. In other cases, the bridge was designed only to support a certain amount of weight and no more.", "probe_text": "Engineers often uncover the reasons behind bridge collapses after conducting thorough investigations. These incidents can be attributed to various factors, including substandard materials used in construction or flaws in critical components. In some instances, bridges are built with specific load-bearing capacities, beyond which they become structurally unsound.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_10-a2_97f76c9e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_10-a2", "base_text": "I used to do a typical five-day week, but after I came out of my parental leave, I decided that I wanted to spend more time with my children before they start school. After negotiating with my boss, we decided to cut my working week down to a three-day work week. This of course meant a significant cut in my pay too, as I'm paid on a pro-rata basis. I've since noticed, though, that my workload hasn't decreased in the slightest! I'm now doing five days' worth of work in three days, but getting paid much less for it!", "probe_text": "Prior to taking parental leave, I was accustomed to a standard five-day workweek. However, upon returning to work, I opted to allocate more time with my children before they begin their formal education. Following discussions with my supervisor, we mutually agreed to reduce my working hours from five days to three, resulting in a substantial decrease in my remuneration due to the pro-rata payment structure. Interestingly, despite this adjustment, my workload remains unchanged – I'm now completing tasks equivalent to a full week's work within just three days, yet receiving significantly less compensation for it.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1603_049b7a72", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1603", "base_text": "Atlantic hurricane seasons Pre-1600 1600s / 10s 1620s / 30s Observation data for years before 1492 is completely unavailable because record keeping was virtually non-existent in the pre-Columbian era, and any records that may have once existed have long since been lost.", "probe_text": "There is no observation data for Atlantic hurricane seasons before 1492, as record keeping was almost nonexistent during the pre-Columbian era, and any potential records from that time have long disappeared.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_10-b1_71cdba65", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_10-b1", "base_text": "I used to do a typical five-day week, but after I came out of my parental leave, I decided that I wanted to spend more time with my children before they start school. After negotiating with my boss, we decided to cut my working week down to a three-day work week. This of course meant a significant cut in my pay too, as I'm paid on a pro-rata basis. I've since noticed, though, that my workload hasn't decreased in the slightest! I'm now doing five days' worth of work in three days, but getting paid much less for it!", "probe_text": "Prior to taking parental leave, I adhered to a standard Monday-to-Friday schedule. However, upon returning to work, I made the conscious decision to allocate more time with my children before they begin their formal education. Following discussions with my supervisor, we mutually agreed to reduce my working hours from five days to three, albeit at a corresponding reduction in remuneration due to my pro-rata compensation structure. Interestingly, despite this adjustment, my workload has not diminished; instead, I'm now completing the equivalent of five days' worth of tasks within a three-day period while earning significantly less for it.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1606_259e2781", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1606", "base_text": "It is generally perceived as upscale and more sophisticated than lad mags, such as Maxim or FHM.", "probe_text": "It is widely regarded as more refined and high-end compared to men's magazines like Maxim or FHM.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_11-a2_e104b766", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_11-a2", "base_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a common language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can result in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could help stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "probe_text": "Business transactions now frequently transcend national boundaries, yet despite English being widely adopted as a global language, variations in communication styles and expectations can be substantial across cultures. Misinterpretations and miscommunications often arise due to unfamiliarity with the cultural norms and customs of business associates from diverse backgrounds. To avoid misunderstandings and cultivate effective working relationships, it's essential to recognize key differences in business etiquette worldwide. Three fundamental areas of variation are particularly noteworthy: understanding these distinctions can significantly enhance your interactions when collaborating with colleagues from different cultures.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1605_3cde9f25", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1605", "base_text": "This sexual imbalance, combined with the effective enslavement of the Tahitian men by the mutineers, led to insurrection and the deaths of most of the men.", "probe_text": "The combination of this gender disparity and the virtual enslavement of the Tahitian men by the mutineers resulted in a rebellion that caused the deaths of the majority of the men.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_11-b1_9167ee66", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_11-b1", "base_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a common language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can result in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could help stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "probe_text": "Global commerce is increasingly taking place across national borders, yet despite English being widely adopted as a common language, variations in business communication norms and expectations persist across cultures. Failure to grasp the cultural nuances of our professional counterparts can lead to misinterpretations, biased assessments, and communication breakdowns. To navigate these differences effectively, consider the following three fundamental areas where business etiquette diverges worldwide:", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1607_6e40ea2d", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1607", "base_text": "Note that Adrastea is now the name of another satellite of Jupiter.", "probe_text": "Be aware that Adrastea currently refers to a different moon of Jupiter.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1610_cfbeb766", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1610", "base_text": "The Golden Gloves are open to all non-professional pugilists age 16 and over.", "probe_text": "Anyone aged 16 or older who is not a professional boxer can participate in the Golden Gloves.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_12-a2_be751e5c", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_12-a2", "base_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language?", "probe_text": "Approximately 100,000 to 50,000 years ago, the earliest signs of human civilization begin to emerge, as exemplified by cave paintings; however, the link between this phenomenon and the development of language remains a mystery. Notably, brain size didn't undergo an abrupt increase, yet humans became significantly more sophisticated and intelligent. The question arises: did the use of language trigger the evolution of their brains, or was it the other way around – that is, were their more complex brains the catalyst for the emergence of language?", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1612_ee48c437", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1612", "base_text": "Whedon, Firefly Companion, Vol 1, 6 Whedon wanted to develop a show about the tactile nature of life, a show where existence was more physical and more difficult.", "probe_text": "According to Whedon in Firefly Companion, Vol 1, page 6, he aimed to create a series that focused on the tangible aspects of living, emphasizing a world where life was tougher and more grounded in physical reality.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1615_1f305c15", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1615", "base_text": "By 1870, more than 2,000 children were being accommodated in five homes.", "probe_text": "By 1870, five homes were housing over 2,000 children.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_12-b1_cd013dd1", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_12-b1", "base_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language?", "probe_text": "Around 100,000 to 50,000 years ago, the emergence of early human societies becomes visible through artefacts like cave paintings; however, the relationship between this development and the origin of language remains a mystery. Despite no noticeable increase in brain size, humans began to exhibit greater complexity and intelligence. The question arises: did the use of language drive the evolution of their brains, or was it their more sophisticated cerebral capacity that gave rise to linguistic capabilities?", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1616_d87b2ab3", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1616", "base_text": "To score consistent hits at medium or long range, players must aim using the iron sights on their guns.", "probe_text": "Players need to use the iron sights on their weapons to reliably land shots at medium or long distances.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1617_31016e3b", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1617", "base_text": "Individuals have also illegally destroyed some trees and are suspected of introducing insect pests from Australia which attack the trees.", "probe_text": "Some people have unlawfully cut down certain trees and are believed to have brought in insect pests from Australia that harm the trees.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_13-a2_f54f01e5", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_13-a2", "base_text": "Many of the major supermarket chains have come under fire with accusations of various unethical acts over the past decade. They've wasted tonnes of food, they've underpaid their suppliers and they've contributed to excessive plastic waste in their packaging, which has had its impact on our environment. But supermarkets and grocers are starting to sit up and take notice. In response to growing consumer backlash against the huge amounts of plastic waste generated by plastic packaging, some of the largest UK supermarkets have signed up to a pact promising to transform packaging and cut plastic wastage.", "probe_text": "Over the past ten years, several prominent supermarket groups have faced intense criticism for their involvement in numerous questionable practices. Specifically, they've been accused of squandering massive amounts of food, exploiting their suppliers by paying them substandard wages, and perpetuating a culture of excessive plastic use through their packaging, which has had far-reaching consequences for the environment. However, it appears that supermarkets are beginning to take heed of consumer discontent over the staggering quantities of plastic waste generated by their packaging. In response to mounting public pressure, several leading UK supermarkets have joined forces with an initiative aimed at revolutionizing their packaging and significantly reducing plastic waste.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1618_fcf07e88", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1618", "base_text": "The candy cane is a traditional candy surrounding the Christmas holiday, particularly in the Western world, although it is possible to find them throughout the year.", "probe_text": "The candy cane is a classic sweet associated with Christmas, especially in Western countries, though it can also be found year-round.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1619_346ee7aa", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1619", "base_text": "The 1974 Atlantic hurricane season officially began on June 1, 1974, and lasted until November 30, 1974.", "probe_text": "The official dates for the 1974 Atlantic hurricane season were from June 1 to November 30, 1974.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_13-b1_1849cd8d", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_13-b1", "base_text": "Many of the major supermarket chains have come under fire with accusations of various unethical acts over the past decade. They've wasted tonnes of food, they've underpaid their suppliers and they've contributed to excessive plastic waste in their packaging, which has had its impact on our environment. But supermarkets and grocers are starting to sit up and take notice. In response to growing consumer backlash against the huge amounts of plastic waste generated by plastic packaging, some of the largest UK supermarkets have signed up to a pact promising to transform packaging and cut plastic wastage.", "probe_text": "Over the past decade, several prominent supermarket chains have faced intense criticism for their involvement in numerous questionable practices. Specifically, they've been accused of squandering vast quantities of food, exploiting their suppliers by paying them subpar wages, and perpetuating an alarming amount of plastic waste through their packaging methods, which has had a profoundly detrimental effect on the environment. However, it appears that supermarkets are beginning to take heed of consumer discontent regarding the staggering amounts of plastic waste generated by their packaging. In response to mounting public pressure, several leading UK supermarkets have joined forces with a pact aimed at revolutionizing their packaging and significantly reducing plastic waste.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1620_5b8b8a1c", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1620", "base_text": "Moenjodaro is situated 7 km away in East-South of the Dokri town.", "probe_text": "Moenjodaro is located 7 kilometers to the east-south of Dokri town.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1622_3670829f", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1622", "base_text": "Koxinga proceeded to devote himself to building Taiwan into an effective base for anti-Qing Dynasty sympathizers who wanted to restore the Ming Dynasty to power.", "probe_text": "Koxinga dedicated his efforts to transforming Taiwan into a stronghold for supporters of the Ming Dynasty seeking to overthrow the Qing Dynasty and restore Ming rule.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_14-a2_870e0b8e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_14-a2", "base_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few people in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "probe_text": "As a young girl growing up in Bangladesh, Wasfia Nazreen's initial encounter with a hula hoop was through a visiting foreign child who was enthusiastically spinning one around. Witnessing this spectacle, Wasfia stood by, observing the scene unfold, as societal norms in her country dictated that girls should refrain from engaging in such activities, including playing with hula hoops or riding bicycles. Fast forward to today, and Wasfia has become a trailblazer of sorts, joining an elite group of individuals who have successfully conquered the Seven Summits – a feat that includes scaling Everest and Kilimanjaro – and holds the distinction of being the first person to incorporate hula-hooping into her climbs. Her motivation behind this remarkable achievement lies in empowering women and girls from a country where they are often discouraged from participating in sports, thereby challenging traditional norms and paving the way for change.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1623_3c4ef269", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1623", "base_text": "References External links 121 Hermione and S / 2002 (121) 1, orbit data website maintained by F. Marchis.", "probe_text": "Sources Outside links 121 Hermione and S / 2002 (121) 1, orbital information site managed by F. Marchis.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1625_03d7a0a5", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1625", "base_text": "Inductors are also employed in electrical transmission systems, where they are used to depress voltages from lightning strikes and to limit switching currents and fault current.", "probe_text": "Inductors are utilized in electrical transmission networks to reduce voltages caused by lightning strikes and to restrict both switching currents and fault currents.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_14-b1_2a18df37", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_14-b1", "base_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few people in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "probe_text": "As a child growing up in Bangladesh, Wasfia Nazreen's initial encounter with a hula hoop was an intriguing one - she observed a visiting foreign youngster effortlessly spinning the hoop. At that time, cultural norms in her homeland dictated that girls should refrain from engaging in such activities, and so Wasfia stood by, observing rather than participating. Today, this same individual has achieved a remarkable feat: becoming one of only a handful of people to have conquered all Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, while also making history as the first person to hula-hoop on each of these towering peaks. Her motivation for undertaking such an extraordinary challenge was rooted in her desire to empower women and girls in a society that discourages them from participating in sports.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1627_033629b7", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1627", "base_text": "Gorani avoids discussing her political and religious views, citing the need for professional neutrality.", "probe_text": "Gorani refrains from sharing her political and religious opinions, explaining that maintaining professional neutrality is necessary.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1628_c7ec83e6", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1628", "base_text": "Alcazar have taken part in Melodifestivalen, the annual competition that selects Sweden's entries for the Eurovision Song Contest, on numerous occasions.", "probe_text": "Alcazar have participated several times in Melodifestivalen, the yearly contest that determines Sweden's representatives for the Eurovision Song Contest.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_15-a2_05b72126", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_15-a2", "base_text": "On the basis of these findings, we recommend that Girox Foods adopt a more people-oriented management style. As part of this, we should explore ways of offering more flexible working hours to our employees and consider how we can enable employees to work from their chosen locations. Managers need to consider a variety of ways to challenge our staff and provide more positive reinforcement and recognition of the work they do. Increased investment in professional development, especially in the area of social and intercultural communication, could also contribute to creating a positive environment for employees to produce their best work.", "probe_text": "Given these results, we propose that Girox Foods shift towards a more employee-centric management approach. This entails examining possibilities for flexible working schedules and exploring how staff can operate remotely from preferred locations. To foster growth and motivation among our personnel, managers should devise diverse strategies to engage and motivate employees, as well as provide regular acknowledgement of their accomplishments. Investing in professional development opportunities, particularly those focusing on social and intercultural skills, could also play a significant role in creating an environment where employees feel empowered to excel in their roles.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1629_fd08c002", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1629", "base_text": "Rainfall comes only 2 - 3 times a year, never exceeding 20 mm.", "probe_text": "It rains just two or three times annually, and the amount never surpasses 20 mm.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_15-b1_cf7d8f73", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_15-b1", "base_text": "On the basis of these findings, we recommend that Girox Foods adopt a more people-oriented management style. As part of this, we should explore ways of offering more flexible working hours to our employees and consider how we can enable employees to work from their chosen locations. Managers need to consider a variety of ways to challenge our staff and provide more positive reinforcement and recognition of the work they do. Increased investment in professional development, especially in the area of social and intercultural communication, could also contribute to creating a positive environment for employees to produce their best work.", "probe_text": "Given these results, we suggest that Girox Foods shift towards a more employee-centric management approach. This involves examining ways to offer flexible working schedules and exploring the possibility of remote work arrangements, allowing staff to choose where they operate from. To foster growth and motivation among employees, managers should develop diverse strategies for engaging them and providing constructive feedback and acknowledgement of their contributions. Investing in professional development programs, particularly those focused on social and intercultural skills, would also be beneficial in creating an environment conducive to peak performance.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_16-a2_b9e9c062", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_16-a2", "base_text": "In the last two centuries, improvements in technology and health meant fewer children died young, fuelling rapid population growth. These large families produced even more children who survived into adulthood and had their own children. But with the wider availability of contraception in the 1960s, the global average number of babies per woman has declined from six babies per woman to as low as two.", "probe_text": "Over the past two centuries, advancements in technology and healthcare led to a significant decrease in infant mortality rates, resulting in accelerated population growth. As a result, families with numerous children were able to produce even more offspring who reached adulthood and went on to have their own children. However, the widespread availability of birth control measures in the 1960s led to a substantial drop in the global average number of births per woman, from six to as few as two.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1633_26a57e3b", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1633", "base_text": "Structure and rules A match between two opponents consists of up to eleven alternating rounds of boxing and chess sessions, starting with a four-minute chess round followed by three minutes of boxing and so on.", "probe_text": "Format and regulations A contest involving two competitors is made up of as many as eleven alternating rounds that switch between chess and boxing, beginning with a four-minute chess session, then three minutes of boxing, and continuing in this pattern.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_16-b1_2312ae86", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_16-b1", "base_text": "In the last two centuries, improvements in technology and health meant fewer children died young, fuelling rapid population growth. These large families produced even more children who survived into adulthood and had their own children. But with the wider availability of contraception in the 1960s, the global average number of babies per woman has declined from six babies per woman to as low as two.", "probe_text": "Over the past two hundred years, advancements in technology and healthcare have led to a significant reduction in infant mortality rates, resulting in accelerated population growth. As a result, families with multiple children grew even larger, producing an additional generation of offspring who reached adulthood and eventually became parents themselves. However, the increased accessibility of birth control measures in the 1960s has reversed this trend, causing the global average number of births per woman to plummet from six to as few as two.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1636_55971ca3", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1636", "base_text": "After these \"rebellions\", land speculators and other non-Métis effectively deprived the Métis of land by exploiting a government program for its purchase, with the government perhaps turning a blind eye.", "probe_text": "Following these \"rebellions,\" land speculators and other non-Métis individuals effectively dispossessed the Métis of their land by taking advantage of a government land purchase program, while the government may have ignored their actions.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1637_4bc6b2ca", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1637", "base_text": "It is revealed that French museums had nearly 2,000 pieces of art that had been stolen by Nazis.", "probe_text": "It is disclosed that almost 2,000 artworks in French museums had been looted by the Nazis.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_17-a2_f6cb84fe", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_17-a2", "base_text": "Having an increased awareness of the possible differences in expectations and behaviour can help us avoid cases of miscommunication, but it is vital that we also remember that cultural stereotypes can be detrimental to building good business relationships. Although national cultures could play a part in shaping the way we behave and think, we are also largely influenced by the region we come from, the communities we associate with, our age and gender, our corporate culture and our individual experiences of the world. The knowledge of the potential differences should therefore be something we keep at the back of our minds, rather than something that we use to pigeonhole the individuals of an entire nation.", "probe_text": "Recognizing the disparities in anticipated conduct and behavior can prevent misunderstandings from arising, yet it's crucial not to overlook the fact that cultural generalizations can undermine the establishment of strong business connections. While national cultures may contribute to our mannerisms and thought processes, we are also significantly influenced by our geographical location, social circles, age, sex, corporate environment, and personal experiences. It is essential to keep in mind the potential variations without using them as a basis for categorizing an entire nation's people.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_17-b1_396e88f6", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_17-b1", "base_text": "Having an increased awareness of the possible differences in expectations and behaviour can help us avoid cases of miscommunication, but it is vital that we also remember that cultural stereotypes can be detrimental to building good business relationships. Although national cultures could play a part in shaping the way we behave and think, we are also largely influenced by the region we come from, the communities we associate with, our age and gender, our corporate culture and our individual experiences of the world. The knowledge of the potential differences should therefore be something we keep at the back of our minds, rather than something that we use to pigeonhole the individuals of an entire nation.", "probe_text": "Recognizing the disparities in expectations and conduct can prevent misunderstandings from arising, yet it is essential to acknowledge that cultural generalizations can undermine the development of strong business connections. While a country's culture may contribute to our behavior and thought patterns, we are also significantly influenced by our geographical location, social circles, age, gender, corporate environment, and personal experiences. It is crucial to keep in mind the potential differences rather than using them as a basis for stereotyping an entire nation.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1640_ae6a393a", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1640", "base_text": "Libpurple has support for many commonly used instant messaging protocols, allowing the user to log into various different services from one application.", "probe_text": "Libpurple is compatible with numerous popular instant messaging protocols, enabling users to access multiple services through a single application.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1641_6939b5c5", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1641", "base_text": "Punk rock has distinguished itself from other non-mainstream genres by self-asserting an active anti-mainstream social movement that resists commercialism and corporate control.", "probe_text": "Punk rock sets itself apart from other alternative genres by actively promoting an anti-mainstream social movement that opposes commercialism and corporate dominance.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_18-a2_80f768b3", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_18-a2", "base_text": "Unlike many other best-selling album artists, Springsteen is still releasing chart-topping, stadium-filling new music and remains at the top of his game in his late 60s. It doesn't surprise me at all. This is a man who tells us our most fundamental stories about ourselves and, when you listen to Born in the USA, those stories are as relevant today as they ever were.", "probe_text": "In stark contrast to many of his peers who have achieved chart-topping success with their albums, Springsteen continues to produce new music that dominates the charts and sells out stadiums well into his 60s. This is hardly a surprise given his enduring ability to craft songs that tap into our collective psyche and resonate deeply with listeners. Take Born in the USA, for instance - its themes remain just as pertinent today as they were when the album was first released.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1642_d6ac262f", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1642", "base_text": "All other subjects may be sat in either Ordinary or Higher Levels.", "probe_text": "All remaining subjects can be taken at either the Ordinary or Higher Level.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_18-b1_897a3049", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_18-b1", "base_text": "Unlike many other best-selling album artists, Springsteen is still releasing chart-topping, stadium-filling new music and remains at the top of his game in his late 60s. It doesn't surprise me at all. This is a man who tells us our most fundamental stories about ourselves and, when you listen to Born in the USA, those stories are as relevant today as they ever were.", "probe_text": "In contrast to many other successful musicians whose popularity has waned with age, Springsteen continues to produce hit music that fills stadiums and tops the charts well into his late sixties. This is hardly a surprise, given his remarkable ability to craft songs that speak directly to our core experiences and values. As evidenced by Born in the USA, the themes he explores remain as timely and relatable today as they were when the album was first released.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1645_8f052d5c", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1645", "base_text": "On a larger scale, mitotic cell division can create progeny from multicellular organisms, such as plants that grow from cuttings.", "probe_text": "On a broader level, mitotic cell division allows multicellular organisms to produce offspring, as seen in plants that develop from cuttings.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_19-a2_6b9ed9bf", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_19-a2", "base_text": "More questions lie in looking at the influence of genetics on brain and language development. Are there genes that mutated and gave us language ability? Researchers have found a gene mutation that occurred between 200,000 and 100,000 years ago, which seems to have a connection with speaking and how our brains control our mouths and face. Monkeys have a similar gene, but it did not undergo this mutation. It's too early to say how much influence genes have on language, but one day the answers might be found in our DNA.", "probe_text": "The relationship between genetics and the emergence of brain and linguistic capabilities remains an area ripe for exploration. Do specific genetic mutations hold the key to unlocking human language abilities? Studies suggest that a gene mutation occurred approximately 200,000 to 100,000 years ago, which appears to be linked to speech development and the neural control of facial expressions. Interestingly, this mutation is not present in our primate cousins, suggesting a divergence in evolutionary pathways. While it's premature to quantify the extent of genetic influence on language, future discoveries may ultimately reveal the secrets hidden within our DNA.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1644_fbd93756", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1644", "base_text": "Ofelia's stepfather, the Falangist Captain Vidal, viciously hunts the Spanish Maquis, guerrillas who fight against the Franco regime in the region, while Ofelia's pregnant mother grows increasingly ill.", "probe_text": "Captain Vidal, Ofelia’s stepfather and a ruthless Falangist, relentlessly pursues the Spanish Maquis—guerrilla fighters resisting Franco’s rule in the area—as Ofelia’s expectant mother’s health steadily declines.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_19-b1_2e5e9ae0", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_19-b1", "base_text": "More questions lie in looking at the influence of genetics on brain and language development. Are there genes that mutated and gave us language ability? Researchers have found a gene mutation that occurred between 200,000 and 100,000 years ago, which seems to have a connection with speaking and how our brains control our mouths and face. Monkeys have a similar gene, but it did not undergo this mutation. It's too early to say how much influence genes have on language, but one day the answers might be found in our DNA.", "probe_text": "The role of genetics in shaping brain and language development remains an area of ongoing inquiry. Is there a specific genetic mutation that enabled humans to acquire language? Studies suggest that a gene alteration occurred between 200,000 and 100,000 years ago, which appears to be linked to the emergence of spoken communication and its neural control mechanisms. Interestingly, this mutation is not present in our primate cousins, despite their possession of a similar gene. While it's premature to quantify the extent of genetic influence on language acquisition, future research may uncover answers by examining the human genome.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1648_73f36813", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1648", "base_text": "Styles There are many different apron forms depending on the purpose of the apron.", "probe_text": "Varieties There are numerous apron styles based on the intended use of the apron.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_TSAR_20-a2_49467e52", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_20-a2", "base_text": "Julie Wong is a leading researcher in the field of Robotics and AI. She has been published extensively as author and co-author of over 50 papers in highly regarded, peer-reviewed journals. She frequently speaks at international conferences and was awarded the prestigious Royal Academy Simone Fielding fellowship in 2012. Julie lives with her family in a smart home she designed herself.", "probe_text": "Julie Wong is a prominent figure in robotics and artificial intelligence research, boasting an impressive publication record as both lead author and co-author of more than 50 scholarly papers in top-tier, peer-reviewed publications. A sought-after speaker at global conferences, Julie was honored with the esteemed Royal Academy Simone Fielding fellowship in 2012 for her outstanding contributions to the field. In addition to her professional accomplishments, Julie resides in a cutting-edge smart home that she personally conceptualized and designed for her family's comfort.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0001_bdf5a5cb", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0001", "base_text": "Jeddah is the principal gateway to Mecca, Islam's holiest city, which able-bodied Muslims are required to visit at least once in their lifetime.", "probe_text": "Mecca, the most revered site in Islam, can only be accessed through Jeddah, a crucial entry point that millions of physically capable Muslims strive to reach at least once during their lifetime.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0002_f1016ecc", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0002", "base_text": "The Great Dark Spot is thought to represent a hole in the methane cloud deck of Neptune.", "probe_text": "A dark anomaly on Neptune's atmosphere is believed to signify an opening within its upper layer of methane clouds.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1647_055cc074", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1647", "base_text": "Also, please do your best to always fill in the edit summary field.", "probe_text": "Additionally, make sure to consistently complete the edit summary section.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
