{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0035_90c434a5", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0035", "base_text": "It is theoretically possible that the other editors who may have reported you, and the administrator who blocked you, are part of a conspiracy against someone half a world away they've never met in person.", "probe_text": "Theoretically, it's conceivable that those other editors who might have flagged you for attention, along with the administrator who took action against you, could be unwitting participants in a far-reaching scheme targeting an individual on the opposite side of the globe whom they've never encountered face-to-face.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_03-a2_550c44ad", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_03-a2", "base_text": "The Hunger Games are an annual event, which the Capitol uses to remind the districts that they are being punished for rebelling. Every year one boy and one girl aged 12 to 18 are chosen from each district by lottery to compete in a battle in which only one person can survive. The chosen teenagers are called \"tributes\". The whole nation is forced to watch the event on television.", "probe_text": "As a yearly occurrence, the Capitol stages the Hunger Games to serve as a constant reminder of the districts’ failed uprising and subsequent penalty. A boy and a girl between the ages of twelve and eighteen are randomly selected from each district to fight to the death, with only a single victor permitted. These selected youths are known as “tributes,” and the entire country is compelled to view the spectacle on television.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1737_df5d83d3", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1737", "base_text": "In the case of asteroids, so many have been discovered that many will never be named by their discoverers.", "probe_text": "When it comes to asteroids, such a large number have been found that most will not be named by those who discovered them.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
