{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1750_33fcc120", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1750", "base_text": "Some define the hadopelagic as waters below 6,000 m (19,685 ft), whether in a trench or not.", "probe_text": "The hadopelagic is sometimes described as any water deeper than 6,000 meters (19,685 feet), regardless of whether it is inside a trench.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0041_069daf86", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0041", "base_text": "Each entry has a datum (a nugget of data) which is a copy of the datum in some backing store.", "probe_text": "Every record contains a duplicate of information stored elsewhere, referred to as a piece of data or an item of factual content.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_TSAR_12-b1_b775b358", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_12-b1", "base_text": "Between 100,000 and 50,000 years ago, though, we start to see the evidence of early human civilisation, through cave paintings for example; no one knows the connection between this and language. Brains didn't suddenly get bigger, yet humans did become more complex and more intelligent. Was it using language that caused their brains to develop? Or did their more complex brains start producing language?", "probe_text": "Around 100,000 to 50,000 years ago, signs of early human civilization begin to emerge, as seen in cave paintings, for instance; however, the link between these developments and the origin of language remains unclear. Although there was no abrupt increase in brain size, humans did exhibit increased complexity and intelligence. It is uncertain whether the use of language drove the advancement of their brains or if their growing cognitive abilities led to the creation of language.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1749_3d6a636a", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1749", "base_text": "Though he was raised in a devout Lutheran household, Bergman later stated that he lost his faith at age eight years, and only came to terms with this fact while making Winter Light.", "probe_text": "Although Bergman grew up in a deeply religious Lutheran family, he later revealed that he lost his faith at the age of eight, and did not fully accept this until he was working on Winter Light.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1752_69261e88", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1752", "base_text": "Before Snow White, the Disney studio had been primarily involved in the production of animated short subjects in the Mickey Mouse and Silly Symphonies series.", "probe_text": "Prior to Snow White, Disney mainly focused on creating animated short films for the Mickey Mouse and Silly Symphonies series.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0042_242200ba", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0042", "base_text": "As a result, although many mosques will not enforce violations, both men and women when attending a mosque must adhere to these guidelines.", "probe_text": "In consequence, while numerous mosques may choose not to penalize infractions, all individuals, regardless of gender, are expected to comply with the established rules upon entering any mosque.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1755_7dc9bde5", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1755", "base_text": "The term Dakshinachara (Right-Hand Path) is used to refer to Tantric sects that do not engage in these heterodox practices.", "probe_text": "Dakshinachara, or the Right-Hand Path, refers to Tantric groups that avoid participating in these unconventional practices.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1753_47158631", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1753", "base_text": "Strength of the bond The atoms in metals have a strong attractive force between them.", "probe_text": "Bond strength The atoms within metals are held together by a powerful force of attraction.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
