{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1759_ae62afab", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1759", "base_text": "Within the hCard is a Geo microformat, which additionally makes the coordinates (latitude & longitude) parsable, so that they can be, say, looked up on a map, or downloaded to a GPS unit.", "probe_text": "The hCard contains a Geo microformat, which also allows the coordinates (latitude and longitude) to be parsed, enabling them to be, for example, displayed on a map or transferred to a GPS device.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1760_a44fc7da", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1760", "base_text": "The Sahara Pump Theory is a hypothesis that explains how flora and fauna left Africa to penetrate the Middle East and then Europe and Asia.", "probe_text": "The Sahara Pump Theory is a proposed explanation for how plants and animals migrated out of Africa into the Middle East, and subsequently into Europe and Asia.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_01-b1_2eff6fe8", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_01-b1", "base_text": "Now NASA is working towards logging some of the smaller asteroids, those measuring 140 metres wide or more. Of the 25,000 estimated asteroids of this size, so far about 8,000 have been logged, leaving 17,000 unaccounted for. Considering that a 19-metre asteroid that exploded above the city of Chelyabinsk in Russia in 2013 injured 1,200 people, these middle-sized asteroids would be a serious danger if they enter Earth's orbit.", "probe_text": "Currently, NASA is endeavoring to catalogue smaller asteroids – specifically, those with a diameter of 140 metres or greater. Approximately 8,000 of the estimated 25,000 asteroids of this scale have been identified to date, meaning around 17,000 remain undiscovered. Given that an asteroid only 19 metres in size detonated over Chelyabinsk, Russia, in 2013 and caused injuries to 1,200 individuals, asteroids of this intermediate size represent a substantial threat should they cross Earth’s path.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0046_de1d6bd4", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0046", "base_text": "Their granddaughter Hélène Langevin-Joliot is a professor of nuclear physics at the University of Paris, and their grandson Pierre Joliot, who was named after Pierre Curie, is a noted biochemist.", "probe_text": "Hélène Langevin-Joliot, the couple's granddaughter, holds a professorship in nuclear physics at the University of Paris. Their grandson, Pierre Joliot, a distinguished biochemist, bears the name of Pierre Curie as a tribute to his illustrious ancestor.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
