{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1805_ced59bc3", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1805", "base_text": "Etymology and usage Lyric derives from the Greek word lyrikos, meaning \"singing to the lyre\".", "probe_text": "Origin and application The term lyric comes from the Greek word lyrikos, which means \"sung with a lyre.\"", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_04-a2_efd8855a", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_04-a2", "base_text": "Small animals like birds, squirrels, mice and insects are a common sight in many cities and towns. But in recent years, the world's press has been full of reports of wild animals coming into cities in bigger and bigger numbers. There have been bears in Vancouver parks, leopards on the streets of Mumbai and wild pigs in gardens in Berlin. What happens when bigger animals come into our cities? Are they welcome or are they considered a danger or a pest?", "probe_text": "It’s typical to see little creatures such as birds, squirrels, mice, and bugs in most urban and suburban areas. However, news outlets globally have recently highlighted an increasing trend of wildlife entering cities in greater quantities. Examples include bears appearing in Vancouver’s parks, leopards roaming Mumbai’s streets, and wild boars showing up in Berlin gardens. What are the implications of larger animals moving into urban environments? Are they viewed as beneficial, or as threats or nuisances?", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_TSAR_11-a2_2531baf8", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_11-a2", "base_text": "Much of today's business is conducted across international borders, and while the majority of the global business community might share the use of English as a common language, the nuances and expectations of business communication might differ greatly from culture to culture. A lack of understanding of the cultural norms and practices of our business acquaintances can result in unfair judgements, misunderstandings and breakdowns in communication. Here are three basic areas of differences in the business etiquette around the world that could help stand you in good stead when you next find yourself working with someone from a different culture.", "probe_text": "In today's globalized economy, international borders no longer pose a barrier to conducting business, but despite English being widely used as a lingua franca, cultural differences can significantly impact the way business is communicated. Unfamiliarity with the customs and norms of foreign colleagues can lead to misinterpretations, misjudgments, and communication failures. To navigate these challenges effectively, it's essential to understand three key aspects of business etiquette that vary across cultures, providing valuable insights for future collaborations with international partners.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1806_24e53fe7", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1806", "base_text": "Proper saddle care can extend the useful life of a saddle, often for decades.", "probe_text": "Taking good care of a saddle can help it last for many years, sometimes even decades.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0056_efe48f3e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0056", "base_text": "It was discovered by Stephen P. Synnott in images from the Voyager 1 space probe taken on March 5, 1979 while orbiting around Jupiter.", "probe_text": "Stephen P. Synnott made a discovery using images captured by the Voyager 1 spacecraft on March 5, 1979, during its orbital pass around Jupiter.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1812_22d93c18", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1812", "base_text": "Though his father wanted him to continue his training as a goldsmith, he showed such a precocious talent in drawing that he started as an apprentice to Michael Wolgemut at the age of fifteen in 1486.", "probe_text": "Although his father wished for him to pursue his goldsmith training, his remarkable early skill in drawing led him to begin an apprenticeship with Michael Wolgemut when he was fifteen years old in 1486.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0059_55075dbe", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0059", "base_text": "The Apostolic Tradition, attributed to the theologian Hippolytus, attests the singing of Hallel psalms with Alleluia as the refrain in early Christian agape feasts.", "probe_text": "According to the Apostolic Tradition, a theological treatise often associated with Hippolytus, evidence suggests that early Christian gatherings for communal meals, known as agape feasts, featured Hallel psalms accompanied by Alleluia as a recurring chant.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1815_5ea29e1e", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1815", "base_text": "The VC was introduced on 29 January 1856 by Queen Victoria to reward acts of valour during the Crimean War.", "probe_text": "Queen Victoria established the VC on January 29, 1856, to honor deeds of bravery performed in the Crimean War.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0060_73ec36b8", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0060", "base_text": "In return, Rollo swore fealty to Charles, converted to Christianity, and undertook to defend the northern region of France against the incursions of other Viking groups.", "probe_text": "In exchange for this favor, Rollo pledged his loyalty to Charles, renounced his pagan ways by embracing Christianity, and committed to safeguarding northern France from further Viking raids.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1818_a3cc7c71", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1818", "base_text": "Overview It was contested by 12 teams, and SK Admira Wien won the championship.", "probe_text": "Summary Twelve teams competed, with SK Admira Wien emerging as the champions.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0061_a1fddcd7", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0061", "base_text": "Disney received a full-size Oscar statuette and seven miniature ones, presented to him by 10-year-old child actress Shirley Temple.", "probe_text": "Shirley Temple, a young actress who was just ten years old at the time, personally handed over seven small replicas of the prestigious award along with one full-sized Oscar statuette to Disney.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1820_72f32c5b", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1820", "base_text": "By September 1 a cyclonic circulation with a diameter of 690 mile (1115 km) was evident on satellite imagery, well to the southeast of the Cape Verde Islands, and several hurricane forecast models anticipated development and strengthening.", "probe_text": "By September 1, satellite images showed a cyclonic circulation about 690 miles (1,115 km) wide, located far southeast of the Cape Verde Islands, and multiple hurricane forecasting models predicted it would develop and intensify.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_04-b1_8ea2c8b1", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_04-b1", "base_text": "Small animals like birds, squirrels, mice and insects are a common sight in many cities and towns. But in recent years, the world's press has been full of reports of wild animals coming into cities in bigger and bigger numbers. There have been bears in Vancouver parks, leopards on the streets of Mumbai and wild pigs in gardens in Berlin. What happens when bigger animals come into our cities? Are they welcome or are they considered a danger or a pest?", "probe_text": "It’s typical to see little creatures such as birds, squirrels, mice, and bugs in most urban and suburban areas. However, news outlets globally have increasingly reported larger wildlife venturing into cities in growing quantities. Examples include bears appearing in Vancouver’s parks, leopards roaming Mumbai’s streets, and wild boars found in Berlin gardens. What are the implications of these larger animals entering urban environments? Are they viewed as beneficial, or as threats and nuisances?", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0062_02e252da", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0062", "base_text": "This leads to consumer confusion when 220 (1,048,576) bytes is referenced as 1 MB (megabyte) instead of 1 MiB.", "probe_text": "The use of \"1 MB\" to represent 220 (1,048,576) bytes causes consumer misunderstanding because it inaccurately equates megabytes with mebibytes.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
