{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1821_3386ff5c", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1821", "base_text": "The last Mummy film grossed over $102 million in the USA and over $400 million worldwide.", "probe_text": "The most recent Mummy movie earned more than $102 million in the United States and surpassed $400 million globally.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0065_8005a104", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0065", "base_text": "Seventh sons have strong \"knacks\" (specific magical abilities), and seventh sons of seventh sons are both extraordinarily rare and powerful.", "probe_text": "Individuals born as seventh children possess remarkable innate talents, known as \"gifts,\" which set them apart from others. Moreover, the phenomenon of being a seventh child of another seventh child is extremely uncommon, yet imbues these individuals with extraordinary abilities.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_TSAR_14-a2_c2cf3619", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_14-a2", "base_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few people in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "probe_text": "As a child in Bangladesh, Wasfia Nazreen encountered a hula hoop when she observed a visiting foreign youngster playing with it. She stood by hesitantly, observing the scene unfold, since societal norms dictated that girls should refrain from using hula hoops or bicycles in her homeland. Fast forward to today: Wasfia is among an elite group of individuals who have conquered the Seven Summits, including the towering Everest and Kilimanjaro peaks - a feat she accomplished while also hula-hooping at each summit, a first for anyone. Her motivation behind this extraordinary endeavor? To inspire women and girls in her native country to defy convention and participate in sports, despite cultural discouragement.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_05-a2_5db79673", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_05-a2", "base_text": "Potentially Hazardous Asteroids' are rocks close enough to pass within 7.5 million kilometres of Earth's orbit. NASA has created a map of 1,400 PHAs, none of which are expected to be a threat in the next one hundred years. With technology already available, NASA can track these objects and make predictions about possible impact, at which point two defence solutions could be launched.", "probe_text": "Asteroids considered ‘Potentially Hazardous’ are those that approach within 7.5 million kilometers of Earth’s orbital path. NASA has cataloged 1,400 of these PHAs, and current projections indicate none pose a danger for the next century. Utilizing existing technology, NASA monitors these objects and forecasts potential impacts, enabling the deployment of one of two defensive strategies if necessary.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0066_16aa1b48", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0066", "base_text": "Benchmarking conducted by PassMark Software highlights the 2009 version's 52 second install time, 32 second scan time, and 7 MB memory utilization.", "probe_text": "A study carried out by PassMark Software reveals that the 2009 edition requires a 52-second installation period, takes approximately 32 seconds to complete a scan, and consumes around 7 megabytes of memory.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
