{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_TSAR_14-b1_48a27bc6", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_14-b1", "base_text": "Wasfia Nazreen first came across a hula hoop as a young girl, when she saw a foreign child who was visiting her native Bangladesh playing with one. Wasfia reluctantly stood by and watched, as in her country it was believed that girls should not play with hula hoops or ride bikes. Now Wasfia is one of the few people in the world to have climbed the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and the first to have hula-hooped on each peak. Her reason for doing so: to empower women and girls in a country which discourages them from doing sport.", "probe_text": "As a child in Bangladesh, Wasfia Nazreen encountered her first hula hoop when she observed a visiting foreign youngster playing with it, an activity that sparked her curiosity despite being discouraged for local girls. Years later, Wasfia has achieved the remarkable feat of conquering the Seven Summits, including Everest and Kilimanjaro, and uniquely, she has also hula-hooped at each summit. Her motivation behind this endeavor is to inspire women and girls in a society that often restricts their participation in sports, thereby promoting empowerment through her actions.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
