{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0073_51fe6efb", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0073", "base_text": "If there are no strong land use controls, buildings are built along a bypass, converting it into an ordinary town road, and the bypass may eventually become as congested as the local streets it was intended to avoid.", "probe_text": "Without strict regulations governing land development, roads that were designed to be bypasses can quickly lose their purpose, becoming clogged with traffic just like the neighborhood streets they were meant to circumvent.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
