{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0090_cc2b0674", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0090", "base_text": "In 1438 Trevi passed under the temporal rule of the Church as part of the legation of Perugia, and thenceforth its history merges first with that of the States of the Church, then (1860) with the united Kingdom of Italy.", "probe_text": "In 1438, Trevi came under the ecclesiastical jurisdiction of the Church as a territory within the Perugia legation, and from that point forward its narrative became intertwined first with that of the Papal States, subsequently merging in 1860 with the newly formed Kingdom of Italy.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_07-b1_7f9bb614", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_07-b1", "base_text": "The Life of Pi tells the extraordinary story of Pi, a teenage boy from India, who is shipwrecked and finds himself trapped in a lifeboat in the Pacific Ocean with a ferocious tiger. It is the third book by the Canadian author Yann Martel, and was published in 2001. Since then, it has sold over seven million copies worldwide, won several prizes and been translated into 41 languages. Martel is the son of a diplomat and as a child lived in Costa Rica, Canada, France and Mexico.", "probe_text": "Yann Martel’s novel, *Life of Pi*, recounts the incredible experiences of Pi, an adolescent from India who survives a shipwreck and is stranded on a lifeboat in the Pacific, sharing it with a dangerous tiger. Released in 2001, this is Martel’s third book. Globally, it has achieved sales exceeding seven million copies, garnered numerous awards, and appeared in translations across 41 languages. The author, whose father was a diplomat, spent his childhood years living in countries including Costa Rica, Canada, France, and Mexico.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gpt_4_1_ASSET_val_1891_5f0334ad", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gpt-4.1", "base_item_id": "ASSET_val_1891", "base_text": "Fiorito originally produced foot fetish videos but soon moved on to coprophagia.", "probe_text": "Fiorito started out making foot fetish videos, but later transitioned to coprophagia.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0091_6b88c993", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0091", "base_text": "The depression moved inland on the 20th as a circulation devoid of convection, and dissipated the next day over Brazil, where it caused heavy rains and flooding.", "probe_text": "By the 20th, the low-pressure system had shifted from the ocean to land, characterized by an absence of convective activity, before dissipating in Brazil on the following day, resulting in severe precipitation and inundation.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_TSAR_16-a2_26a04842", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_16-a2", "base_text": "In the last two centuries, improvements in technology and health meant fewer children died young, fuelling rapid population growth. These large families produced even more children who survived into adulthood and had their own children. But with the wider availability of contraception in the 1960s, the global average number of babies per woman has declined from six babies per woman to as low as two.", "probe_text": "Over the past couple of centuries, advances in healthcare and technology have significantly reduced child mortality rates, leading to a sharp acceleration in population expansion. As a result, larger families emerged, yielding even more offspring who reached adulthood and went on to have children of their own. However, following the increased accessibility of birth control methods in the 1960s, the worldwide average number of births per woman has dropped substantially, from six to as few as two.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
