{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_16-a2_127cfb76", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_16-a2", "base_text": "In the last two centuries, improvements in technology and health meant fewer children died young, fuelling rapid population growth. These large families produced even more children who survived into adulthood and had their own children. But with the wider availability of contraception in the 1960s, the global average number of babies per woman has declined from six babies per woman to as low as two.", "probe_text": "Over the past 200 years, advances in medicine and technology have resulted in increased child survival rates, leading to a swift rise in the world’s population. These bigger families then went on to have even more children who lived to maturity and started families of their own. However, since the 1960s, with greater access to birth control, the average number of children born to each woman globally has fallen from around six to as few as two.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_ASSET_test_0025_a026daf6", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0025", "base_text": "Despina was discovered in late July, 1989 from the images taken by the Voyager 2 probe.", "probe_text": "Despina's discovery occurred towards the end of July 1989, based on photographs captured by the Voyager 2 spacecraft.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0187_a60e2688", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0187", "base_text": "Samovar & Porter (1994), p. 84 Syrians did not congregate in urban enclaves; many of the immigrants who had worked as peddlers were able to interact with Americans on a daily basis.", "probe_text": "According to Samovar and Porter's study published in 1994, page 84, Syrian immigrants did not typically cluster together in isolated urban areas. Instead, many of the immigrant peddlers who had previously worked among Americans were able to engage with them regularly.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
