{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_18-a2_f3316338", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_18-a2", "base_text": "Unlike many other best-selling album artists, Springsteen is still releasing chart-topping, stadium-filling new music and remains at the top of his game in his late 60s. It doesn't surprise me at all. This is a man who tells us our most fundamental stories about ourselves and, when you listen to Born in the USA, those stories are as relevant today as they ever were.", "probe_text": "Even though numerous popular recording artists have faded from prominence, Springsteen continues to produce successful new songs and consistently performs in large venues, still performing at a peak level despite being in his late 60s – a fact that I find completely unsurprising. He’s an artist who articulates the core narratives of our lives, and the themes within albums like *Born in the USA* feel just as impactful and current now as they always have.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
