{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0215_518ff239", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0215", "base_text": "At four-and-a-half years old he was left to fend for himself on the streets of northern Italy for the next four years, living in various orphanages and roving through towns with groups of other homeless children.", "probe_text": "For nearly five years, a young boy was forced to survive on his own in northern Italy's urban landscape. He spent the subsequent four years shuttling between different orphanages and wandering through towns alongside other destitute youngsters.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_18-b1_61921799", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_18-b1", "base_text": "Unlike many other best-selling album artists, Springsteen is still releasing chart-topping, stadium-filling new music and remains at the top of his game in his late 60s. It doesn't surprise me at all. This is a man who tells us our most fundamental stories about ourselves and, when you listen to Born in the USA, those stories are as relevant today as they ever were.", "probe_text": "Even though a lot of popular musicians who’ve sold millions of albums no longer produce hit records or attract large concert audiences, Springsteen continues to create successful new songs and perform in stadiums, still performing at a peak level despite being in his late 60s – and that’s not at all unexpected. He’s an artist who articulates the core narratives of our lives, and the themes in albums like *Born in the USA* feel just as impactful and current now as they always have.", "target_level": "b1", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 2, "source": "patch_v1"}
