{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_70b_ASSET_test_0054_6ff40e82", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-70b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0054", "base_text": "Weelkes was later to find himself in trouble with the Chichester Cathedral authorities for his heavy drinking and immoderate behaviour.", "probe_text": "Weelkes eventually landed in hot water with the powers that be at Chichester Cathedral due to his excessive drinking habits and unruly conduct.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_gemma_3_27b_TSAR_19-a2_e5fab968", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "gemma-3-27b", "base_item_id": "TSAR_19-a2", "base_text": "More questions lie in looking at the influence of genetics on brain and language development. Are there genes that mutated and gave us language ability? Researchers have found a gene mutation that occurred between 200,000 and 100,000 years ago, which seems to have a connection with speaking and how our brains control our mouths and face. Monkeys have a similar gene, but it did not undergo this mutation. It's too early to say how much influence genes have on language, but one day the answers might be found in our DNA.", "probe_text": "Further inquiry centers on examining how heredity impacts the growth of the brain and the development of language. Did specific genes change over time, ultimately providing us with the capacity for language? Investigations have revealed a genetic mutation—appearing between 200,000 and 100,000 years in the past—that appears linked to speech and the neurological control of facial and mouth movements. While a comparable gene exists in monkeys, they did not experience this particular mutation. Although the extent of genetic influence on language remains unclear, future discoveries may well be located within our DNA.", "target_level": "a2", "dataset": "TSAR2025", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0223_dc2ca958", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0223", "base_text": "Instead, the crew fashioned a trailer with a cantilevered arm attached to the \"hovercraft\" and shot the scene while riding up Templin Highway north of Santa Clarita.", "probe_text": "The team opted for an alternative solution by constructing a trailer equipped with a pivoting extension that was connected to the hovercraft, allowing them to film on location along Templin Highway in the vicinity of Santa Clarita.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
{"probe_id": "patch_sem_llama_3_1_8b_ASSET_test_0226_a5ce03bb", "probe_family": "invariance", "probe_subtype": "semantic", "generator_model": "llama-3.1-8b", "base_item_id": "ASSET_test_0226", "base_text": "A historian has stated that \"it was quinine's efficacy that gave colonists fresh opportunities to swarm into the Gold Coast, Nigeria and other parts of west Africa\".", "probe_text": "Historical records suggest that the potent effects of quinine enabled European settlers to flood into West Africa, specifically the Gold Coast, Nigeria, and surrounding regions.", "target_level": "simpler", "dataset": "ASSET", "tier": 1, "source": "patch_v1"}
